a. Monitoring & Alerting
Implement centralized monitoring for all Workato recipes using:
Workato’s native Monitoring Dashboard (recipe health, job history, error rates).
Integration with enterprise monitoring tools (e.g., Splunk, Datadog, New Relic) via webhooks or API connectors.
Set up real-time alerting on critical failures, SLA breaches, and latency thresholds.
Provide visibility into recipe execution status, retries, and failure reasons.
b. Logging & Audit Trails
Ensure structured, correlated logs for all transactions with unique request/trace IDs.
Enable detailed error logging capturing input payloads, stack traces, and external system responses.
Retain logs as per compliance requirements (e.g., 90 days for audits).
Provide audit trail access to support and compliance teams.
c. Error Handling & Incident Management
Define standardized error categories and remediation steps.
Configure automatic retries, exponential backoff, and dead-letter queue patterns in Workato recipes.
Integrate with incident management systems (e.g., ServiceNow, PagerDuty) for seamless escalation.
Document incident response playbooks tailored for Workato operational issues.
d. Performance Management
Monitor throughput, processing times, and resource utilization of recipes.
Detect and mitigate bottlenecks via recipe optimization and horizontal scaling.
Implement usage quotas and throttling to prevent backend overload.
e. Configuration & Change Management
Use Workato CLI and version control (Git) to manage recipe versions.
Establish formal change management workflows including code reviews and approvals.
Maintain environment segregation (dev, test, prod) with clear promotion paths.
f. Backup & Disaster Recovery
Document backup strategy for Workato recipes, configurations, and OPA agents.
Define disaster recovery RTO/RPO objectives and test failover procedures.
Maintain cross-region agent deployments for high availability.
2. Onboarding Requirements
a. Developer Onboarding
Provide comprehensive documentation covering:
Workato architecture and key concepts.
Recipe creation, debugging, and deployment procedures.
Authentication methods and security best practices.
Integration patterns and best practices for migration.
Conduct hands-on training workshops and live demo sessions.
Provide sandbox environment access for experimentation.
b. Operations & Support Onboarding
Train support teams on Workato monitoring tools and alert handling.
Share runbooks for common issues, escalation paths, and troubleshooting steps.
Document operational KPIs and SLAs.
Establish a knowledge base or wiki with FAQs and troubleshooting guides.
c. Security & Compliance Training
Educate teams on data privacy, secure handling of credentials, and compliance controls within Workato.
Ensure understanding of encryption, masking, and audit logging features.
d. API Consumer Onboarding
Update API documentation portals with new Workato API endpoints and usage guidelines.
Provide sample requests, authentication steps, and response examples.
Host onboarding webinars or office hours for API consumers.
